  "narrative": "No assessments are due and independent validation capacity is exhausted, so this explore stage registers only new within-dataset comparisons. The main unresolved scientific questions after H320 are: (1) quantify the absolute PTEN-loss STAT3 association in high versus lower IFN-gamma contexts rather than only the interaction, especially in TP53-intact cells where p53-MDM2/PTEN-related biology is most directly interpretable and cells are adequately powered; and (2) test whether the IFN-gamma context is specific to PTEN-STAT3 or extends to the larger TP53-USP7, SMARCA4-SMARCA2, MSI-WRN, and KEAP1-NFE2L2 associations, as well as to CDKN2A-MDM2. Existing active claims H325, H326, and H327 remain important: H325 and H326 provide direct all-TP53 high and lower IFN PTEN-STAT3 estimates, and H327 provides the formal CDKN2A-MDM2 IFN interaction. I intentionally avoid highly nested rare-exposure PTEN contexts because the 20-per-cell minimum could make them bounded rather than informative; the new TP53-intact IFN strata are more likely to have adequate exposed cells. For direction -1 mean-difference claims, anticipated_direction -1 encodes a raw exposed-minus-comparator contrast that is negative, meaning the exposed predictor has a more negative dependency score and therefore stronger dependency. For direction -1 interaction claims, anticipated_direction -1 encodes a raw interaction that is negative, meaning the exposed-minus-comparator contrast is more negative in the named subgroup than in its complement. The large-axis IFN interaction claims anticipate raw interaction 0 because IFN-gamma has so far been accepted only as a context modifier for the moderate PTEN-STAT3 axis, not for the large axes. The NFE2L2 interaction uses direction +1 because accepted KEAP1-loss evidence corresponds to less negative NFE2L2 scores, i.e. weaker measured dependency. The MDM2 high IFN plus 9p21-low and high research signature C direct claims test whether biologically plausible CDKN2A locus-context labels and constructed signature-C context combine with IFN context. All results would remain associations in the supplied lung-cell-line CRISPR screen dataset, with no claim of causality or external generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Current accepted framework remains unchanged. The four very large associations are TP53 non-loss-USP7, SMARCA4 loss-SMARCA2, MSI-high-WRN, and KEAP1 loss with weaker measured NFE2L2 dependency. PTEN-STAT3 and CDKN2A-MDM2 are moderate but context-sensitive. H320 accepted a high IFN-gamma interaction for PTEN-STAT3. Current proposals add direct high/lower IFN PTEN-STAT3 estimates in TP53-intact cells, direct high IFN MDM2 context estimates, and formal IFN specificity tests for the large axes. These are the highest-value untested comparisons remaining under the 12-slot analyze budget. Existing active H325/H326/H327 should remain first-priority if slots allow. Further threshold mining should be minimized; future work ideally requires adequate pre-specified external validation followed by mechanistic perturbation."
